            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Who is the consumer of this interface?  Is this considered \"internal\" to entity-manager?  If so, what is the usecase for it?\n\nIf this is not considered internal, why do we not have a PDI definition for this use case?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This is a new method on the xyz.openbmc_project.FruDeviceManager interface which isn't in PDI.  It wasn't an interface that is expected to be called from.... anywhere except a developer or debug shell.  By our current definition I would call that still internal?  I think at one point the idea was that these would get a fru-device CLI wrapped on them so we could do simple debug tasks from the shell, but that never happened (although might be worth an afternoon of my time to go do to make that more obvious).\n\nI'm a little worried that documenting them in PDI will give the wrong idea about their stability or security.  They really shouldn't be used.  The \"I don't want to remember the command to write an eeprom directly\" case might be a minor exception, although I'm not sure even that qualifies.\n\nFWIW, I'm a little suspect about this API being needed at all versus the bytes one we already have."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
